<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Related Work</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Video-to-Audio Generation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Offline video-to-audio (V2A) generation has been explored using both autoregressive (AR) and non-autoregressive (Non-AR) models.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">AR models.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">AR models for V2A have focused on generating discrete audio tokens. One line of work operates on VQ-VAE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib99" title="" class="ltx_ref">van den Oord et al., 2017</a>)</cite> latents derived from Mel-spectrograms, which requires a separate vocoder for waveform synthesis. This category includes SpecVQGAN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Iashin &amp; Rahtu, 2021</a>)</cite>, which uses a transformer to generate code indices from video RGB and optical flow; Im2Wav <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib83" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sheffer &amp; Adi, 2023</a>)</cite>, which adopts a dual-transformer architecture conditioned on CLIP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radford et al., 2021</a>)</cite> features; and CondFoleyGen <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Du et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, which uses ResNet (2+1)D-18 vision encoder <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2016</a>)</cite>. Another line of AR models utilizes discrete tokenizers based on raw waveforms using RVQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Défossez et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kumar et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. In this paradigm, FoleyGen <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mei et al., 2024b</a>)</cite> explores various vision encoders like CLIP and ImageBind <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Girdhar et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, while V-AURA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib101" title="" class="ltx_ref">Viertola et al., 2025</a>)</cite> has achieved state-of-the-art performance in this category by introducing Synchformer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Iashin et al., 2024</a>)</cite> video encoder, which enabled semantic and strong temporal alignment.
The Synchformer’s video encoder, a Motionformer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Patrick et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bertasius et al., 2021</a>)</cite> relies on non-causal attention over video chunks. While suitable for the offline task, this makes V-AURA incompatible with our scope, the frame-level online V2A task.
Our framework, SoundReactor, is categorized in this AR paradigm based on continuous audio latents and is applicable for both the offline and frame-level online V2A tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Non-AR models.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Non-AR models have also been widely investigated.
The first direction involves training models from scratch based on Diffusion Models (DMs) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>)</cite> and Flow-matching Models (FMs) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2023b</a>)</cite>.
For instance, Diff-Foley <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., 2023</a>)</cite> uses a CAVP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., 2023</a>)</cite> vision encoder to train DMs on Mel-spectrogram latents, while MultiFoley <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2025</a>)</cite> applies a similar approach to latents derived from raw waveforms projected by DAC-based VAE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kumar et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
Models such as Frieren <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib104" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024b</a>)</cite> and MMAudio <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite> leverage FMs; Frieren uses CAVP, whereas MMAudio employs a multimodal diffusion transformer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Esser et al., 2024</a>)</cite> with CLIP and Synchformer encoders.
ThinkSound <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> builds upon a multimodal LLM framework that uses Chain-of-Thought reasoning, followed by the MMAudio-style audio generator.
A second direction is training models from scratch based on discrete tokens using MaskGIT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.
VATT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024a</a>)</cite> employs a two-stage pipeline where it first generates a text caption from the video and then uses MaskGIT to predict code indices of EnCodec <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Défossez et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
MaskVAT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pascual et al., 2024</a>)</cite> applies MaskGIT to predict code indices of DAC conditioned on CLIP and SparseSync <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Iashin et al., 2022</a>)</cite> features.
The third major trend is an adaptation of pre-trained text-to-audio models. Several methods steer AudioLDM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2023a</a>)</cite>: ReWaS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jeong et al., 2024</a>)</cite> uses a ControlNet-based approach <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib108" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2023</a>)</cite> with an energy curve from the Synchformer; V2A-Mapper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib103" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024a</a>)</cite> employs a lightweight network to map CLIP embeddings to CLAP embeddings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib105" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu* et al., 2023</a>)</cite>; Seeing &amp; Hearing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib106" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xing et al., 2024</a>)</cite> conditions the generator using ImageBind as a multimodal aligner; and FoleyCrafter <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib109" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> fine-tunes it using an adapter-based method with CLIP features and a learnable timestamp adapter. Other backbones are also adapted, such as SpecMaskGIT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Comunità et al., 2024</a>)</cite> by SpecMaskFoley <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib110" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhong et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and Stable Audio Open <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Evans et al., 2025</a>)</cite> by CAFA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Benita et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, both using ControlNet with CLIP and Synchformer features.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>AR Audio Generation without Vector Quantization</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our work builds upon the emerging paradigm of AR audio generation with continuous audio latents.
Prior work in this area has focused on unimodal audio domains such as unconditional music generation (CAM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pasini et al., 2024</a>)</cite>) and speech synthesis (DiTAR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jia et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, SALAD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib98" title="" class="ltx_ref">Turetzky et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, MELLE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Meng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>).
Concurrently, CALM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib78" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rouard et al., 2025</a>)</cite> adopts a MAR-style framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite> for speech and music continuation, using a consistency model-based head. Our work is distinct from this prior and concurrent work in two key aspects.
First, to our best knowledge, we are the first to tackle an audio-visual multimodal task within this paradigm, where we introduce and solve the novel task of frame-level online V2A generation (see Section <a href="#S1" title="1 Introduction ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Problem Setup: Frame-level Online Video-to-Audio Generation ‣ 3 SoundReactor ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> for comparison to the offline setup.). Second, regarding diffusion head acceleration, our work is complementary to CALM: we investigate the ECT framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geng et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, in contrast to their sCM-based from-scratch training <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu &amp; Song, 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> SoundReactor-Diffusion’s training</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_align_center ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            Dataset <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">repeat</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
              Sample <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\{\mathbf{x}_{1}^{0},\dots,\mathbf{x}_{n}^{0}\},\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{v}_{n}\})\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\{\mathbf{x}_{1}^{0},\dots,\mathbf{x}_{n}^{0}\},\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{v}_{n}\})\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim p(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim p(t)</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln~t\sim\mathcal{N}(P_{\text{mean}},P_{\text{std}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.497em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mean</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>std</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln~t\sim\mathcal{N}(P_{\text{mean}},P_{\text{std}})</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{v}_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{v}_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg1.l4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>: null-embedding
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{i}^{0}+t\,\bm{\epsilon}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{i}^{0}+t\,\bm{\epsilon}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}\leftarrow F_{\bm{\phi}}(\mathbf{v}_{\leq i},\,\mathbf{x}^{0}_{&lt;i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}\leftarrow F_{\bm{\phi}}(\mathbf{v}_{\leq i},\,\mathbf{x}^{0}_{&lt;i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{Stage1}}(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})\;\leftarrow\;\lambda(t)e^{-u_{\bm{\theta}}(t)}\;\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\big\|\mathbf{x}_{i}^{0}-D_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t},t,\mathbf{z}_{i})\big\|_{2}^{2}+u_{\bm{\theta}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>Stage1</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{Stage1}}(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})\;\leftarrow\;\lambda(t)e^{-u_{\bm{\theta}}(t)}\;\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\big\|\mathbf{x}_{i}^{0}-D_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t},t,\mathbf{z}_{i})\big\|_{2}^{2}+u_{\bm{\theta}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              Update <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})\leftarrow(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})-\eta\,\nabla_{(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})}\mathcal{L}_{\text{Stage1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>Stage1</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})\leftarrow(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})-\eta\,\nabla_{(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})}\mathcal{L}_{\text{Stage1}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">until</span> converged

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> SoundReactor-ECT’s training</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_align_center ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            Dataset <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, pretrained parameters <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{\bm{\theta}},\tilde{\bm{\phi}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{\bm{\theta}},\tilde{\bm{\phi}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
mapping <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(r\mid t,\mathrm{Iters})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Iters</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(r\mid t,\mathrm{Iters})</annotation></semantics></math>,
weighting function <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, metric function <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>,

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Init:</span> <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})\leftarrow(\tilde{\bm{\theta}},\tilde{\bm{\phi}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})\leftarrow(\tilde{\bm{\theta}},\tilde{\bm{\phi}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Iters}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Iters</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Iters}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">repeat</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              Sample <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\{\mathbf{x}_{1}^{0},\dots,\mathbf{x}_{n}^{0}\},\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{v}_{n}\})\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\{\mathbf{x}_{1}^{0},\dots,\mathbf{x}_{n}^{0}\},\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{v}_{n}\})\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              Sample <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim p(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim p(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\sim m(r\mid t,\mathrm{Iters})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Iters</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\sim m(r\mid t,\mathrm{Iters})</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg2.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg2.l5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln~t\sim\mathcal{N}(P_{\text{mean}},P_{\text{std}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.497em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mean</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>std</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln~t\sim\mathcal{N}(P_{\text{mean}},P_{\text{std}})</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{v}_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{v}_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg2.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg2.l6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg2.l6.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg2.l6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>: null-embedding
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{t}_{i}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{i}^{0}+t\,\bm{\epsilon}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{t}_{i}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{i}^{0}+t\,\bm{\epsilon}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,  <math id="alg2.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{r}_{i}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{i}^{0}+r\,\bm{\epsilon}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{r}_{i}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}_{i}^{0}+r\,\bm{\epsilon}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,  <math id="alg2.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t\leftarrow t-r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t\leftarrow t-r</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{Stage2}}({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})\leftarrow w(t)\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}d\!\left(G_{({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})}(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t}),\,G_{\mathrm{sg}({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})}(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{r})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>Stage2</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.350em;" width="0.350em"><mi>d</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{Stage2}}({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})\leftarrow w(t)\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}d\!\left(G_{({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})}(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t}),\,G_{\mathrm{sg}({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})}(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{r})\right)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> sg: stop-gradient
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})\leftarrow({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})-\eta\,\nabla_{({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})}\mathcal{L}_{\text{Stage2}}({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>Stage2</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})\leftarrow({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})-\eta\,\nabla_{({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})}\mathcal{L}_{\text{Stage2}}({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{sg}({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})\leftarrow\mathrm{stopgrad}(\mu\,\mathrm{sg}({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})+(1-\mu\,)({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sg</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{sg}({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})\leftarrow\mathrm{stopgrad}(\mu\,\mathrm{sg}({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})+(1-\mu\,)({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}}))</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l10.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg2.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>: EMA rate
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Iters}\leftarrow\mathrm{Iters}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Iters</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Iters</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Iters}\leftarrow\mathrm{Iters}+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">until</span> <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{\theta}},{\bm{\phi}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> SoundReactor’s frame-level online V2A sampling</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            Video frames <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{V_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{V_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> (Raw videos); vision encoding module <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>; transformer <math id="alg3.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\bm{\phi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\bm{\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math>; diffusion head <math id="alg3.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>; waveform decoder <math id="alg3.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Dec}_{\text{VAE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Dec</mi><mtext>VAE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Dec}_{\text{VAE}}</annotation></semantics></math>; null embedding <math id="alg3.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math>; guidance scale <math id="alg3.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>; head mode <math id="alg3.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{mode}\in\{\mathtt{Diffusion},\mathtt{ECT}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚖𝚘𝚍𝚎</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝙳𝚒𝚏𝚏𝚞𝚜𝚒𝚘𝚗</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙴𝙲𝚃</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{mode}\in\{\mathtt{Diffusion},\mathtt{ECT}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{0}_{0}\leftarrow\texttt{&lt;BOS&gt;}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">&lt;BOS&gt;</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{0}_{0}\leftarrow\texttt{&lt;BOS&gt;}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1\ldots n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1\ldots n</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i-1}\leftarrow F_{\bm{\phi}}(\mathbf{x}^{0}_{i-1};\mathbf{v}_{\leq i-1},\,\mathbf{x}^{0}_{&lt;i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i-1}\leftarrow F_{\bm{\phi}}(\mathbf{x}^{0}_{i-1};\mathbf{v}_{\leq i-1},\,\mathbf{x}^{0}_{&lt;i-1})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}(V_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}(V_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{cond}},\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}}]\leftarrow F_{\bm{\phi}}([\mathbf{v}_{i},\varnothing];\mathbf{v}_{\leq i-1},\,\mathbf{x}^{0}_{\leq i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>cond</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>null</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{cond}},\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}}]\leftarrow F_{\bm{\phi}}([\mathbf{v}_{i},\varnothing];\mathbf{v}_{\leq i-1},\,\mathbf{x}^{0}_{\leq i-1})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l6.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Batch process for CFG paths
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}\leftarrow\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}}+\omega(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{cond}}-\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>null</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>cond</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>null</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}\leftarrow\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}}+\omega(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{cond}}-\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}\leftarrow\mathrm{Concat}\big(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i-1},\,\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Concat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}\leftarrow\mathrm{Concat}\big(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i-1},\,\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{mode}=\mathtt{Diffusion}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚖𝚘𝚍𝚎</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝙳𝚒𝚏𝚏𝚞𝚜𝚒𝚘𝚗</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{mode}=\mathtt{Diffusion}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg3.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{0}_{i}\leftarrow\mathtt{DiffusionSampling}\!\left(D_{\bm{\theta}},\,\mathbf{z}_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:12.580em;" width="12.580em"><mi>𝙳𝚒𝚏𝚏𝚞𝚜𝚒𝚘𝚗𝚂𝚊𝚖𝚙𝚕𝚒𝚗𝚐</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{0}_{i}\leftarrow\mathtt{DiffusionSampling}\!\left(D_{\bm{\theta}},\,\mathbf{z}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l10.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Multi-step sampling
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg3.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{0}_{i}\leftarrow\mathtt{CMSampling}\!\left(D_{\bm{\theta}},\,\mathbf{z}_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:7.330em;" width="7.330em"><mi>𝙲𝙼𝚂𝚊𝚖𝚙𝚕𝚒𝚗𝚐</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{0}_{i}\leftarrow\mathtt{CMSampling}\!\left(D_{\bm{\theta}},\,\mathbf{z}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l12.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Few-step sampling (NFE=1<math id="alg3.l12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>4)
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{streaming\_decode}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚜𝚝𝚛𝚎𝚊𝚖𝚒𝚗𝚐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚌𝚘𝚍𝚎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{streaming\_decode}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg3.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Dec}_{\text{VAE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Dec</mi><mtext>VAE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Dec}_{\text{VAE}}</annotation></semantics></math> is causal <span id="alg3.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg3.l15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{1:i}\leftarrow\mathrm{Dec}_{\text{VAE}}\!\left(\{\mathbf{x}^{0}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>Dec</mi><mtext>VAE</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{1:i}\leftarrow\mathrm{Dec}_{\text{VAE}}\!\left(\{\mathbf{x}^{0}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l15.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Incremental decoding
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <span id="alg3.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">not</span> <math id="alg3.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{streaming\_decode}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚜𝚝𝚛𝚎𝚊𝚖𝚒𝚗𝚐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚌𝚘𝚍𝚎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{streaming\_decode}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{1:n}\leftarrow\mathrm{Dec}_{\text{VAE}}\!\left(\{\mathbf{x}^{0}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>Dec</mi><mtext>VAE</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{1:n}\leftarrow\mathrm{Dec}_{\text{VAE}}\!\left(\{\mathbf{x}^{0}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l19.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Decode all tokens at once
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> Waveform <math id="alg3.l21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{1:n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{1:n}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<figure id="A2.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F5.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.02110v1/grid_vis_1.png" id="A2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/124;" width="548" height="124" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02110v1/cls_plot_1.svg" id="A2.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/208;" width="548" height="208"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">((a)) </span>Example 1</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F5.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.02110v1/grid_vis_2.png" id="A2.F5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/124;" width="548" height="124" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F5.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02110v1/cls_plot_2.svg" id="A2.F5.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/208;" width="548" height="208"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">((b)) </span>Example 2</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Visualization of DINOv2 grid features and cosine similarity of their [<span id="A2.F5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CLS</span>]-tokens between (A) adjacent frames and (B) every other frame. Visualizations are done by applying PCA to grid features and mapping them to RGB.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Vision token modeling</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt a pretrained DINOv2 vision encoder to extract grid features per video frame.
We use grid features instead of the encoder’s [<span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CLS</span>]-token because it lacks the temporal cues necessary for audio-visual synchronization. Our preliminary analysis, shown in Figure <a href="#A2.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, reveals that the cosine similarities between (A) adjacent video frames (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math>FPS) and (B) every other frame (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math>FPS) are significantly high<span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              The average cosine similarity over <math id="footnote8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3,830" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3,830</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3,830</annotation></semantics></math> video clips in our test split is <math id="footnote8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.99\pm 0.0072" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.99</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.0072</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.99\pm 0.0072</annotation></semantics></math> for adjacent frames and <math id="footnote8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.98\pm 0.010" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.98</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.010</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.98\pm 0.010</annotation></semantics></math> for every other frame.</span></span></span>.
We extract grid features from the final layer before the [<span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CLS</span>]-token head. We employ the <span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dinov2-vits14-reg<span id="footnote9" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">9</span></span>
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                <a href="https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov2" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url">https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov2</a></span></span></span></span> (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="21" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>21</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">21</annotation></semantics></math> M parameters) for better per<span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>frame encoding efficiency than larger backbones.
Since raw grid features might be computationally expensive depending on a budget (e.g., training throughput and data storage), we first apply bilinear interpolation to halve both spatial dimensions. Second, we apply Principal Component Analysis (PCA) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jolliffe, 2011</a>)</cite> to reduce the hidden dimension from the original <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="384" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>384</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">384</annotation></semantics></math>. We use <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="59" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>59</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">59</annotation></semantics></math>, which preserves <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="70\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">70\%</annotation></semantics></math> of the cumulative explained variance (CEV) by default.
These compressed features are precomputed before training. The adjacent frame subtraction is conducted on the precomputed grid features before being fed to the downstream projection layer described in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Modeling Framework ‣ 3 SoundReactor ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 SoundReactor ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> (a).
We use a <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional learnable aggregate token for the transformer aggregator. For the transformer aggregator, we use a single non-causal transformer layer with learnable positional embeddings.
We conduct ablation studies on these vision conditions in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Ablation Study on Vision Conditioning ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Audio token modeling</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the stereo VAE from SA Series <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Evans et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Evans et al., 2024</a>)</cite> as a model backbone.
We change the temporal downsampling rate from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2048</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2048</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1600</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1600</annotation></semantics></math> and train with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>48</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">48</annotation></semantics></math> kHz stereo waveform by using OGameData250K and WavCaps <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mei et al., 2024a</a>)</cite> dataset from scratch.
We follow the original training configuration <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Evans et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
The network parameter size is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="157" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>157</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">157</annotation></semantics></math> M.
In the latent space, we get <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math> dimensions of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math>-Hz continuous audio latents.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multimodal transformer with diffusion head</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the multimodal AR transformer, we use <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>18</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">18</annotation></semantics></math> layers, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1024</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1024</annotation></semantics></math> hidden dimensions, and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> heads.
The model backbone follows LLaMA-style design <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib94" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib95" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023b</a>)</cite>,
applying pre-normalization using RMSNorm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib107" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang &amp; Sennrich, 2019</a>)</cite>, SwiGLU activation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shazeer, 2020</a>)</cite>, and rotary positional embeddings (RoPE) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib89" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
For the diffusion head, we set <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> blocks and a width of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1280" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1280</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1280</annotation></semantics></math> channels.
The architecture of the diffusion head largely follows the original architecture in MAR.
The total parameter size is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="320" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>320</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">320</annotation></semantics></math> M (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="250" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>250</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">250</annotation></semantics></math> M for the transformer and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>70</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">70</annotation></semantics></math> M for the diffusion head). We ablate various numbers of parameters of the diffusion head in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Ablation Study on Generator Training ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Training Details</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stage-1: Diffusion pretraining</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After obtaining <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> through the audio VAE, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is standardized globally to zero mean and standard deviation <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\text{data}}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\text{data}}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> by following EDM2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
We utilize the EDM’s skip connection <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{skip}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>skip</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{skip}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, output scale <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{out}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{out}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, input scale <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{in}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{in}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{noise}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>noise</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{noise}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for modeling <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E9.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.E9.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t},t,\mathbf{z}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\bm{\theta}}(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t},t,\mathbf{z}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.E9.1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{\text{skip}}(t)\,\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t}+c_{\text{out}}(t)\,\text{NN}_{\bm{\theta}}\big(c_{\text{in}}(t)\,\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t},c_{\text{noise}}(t),\mathbf{z}_{i}\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>skip</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>NN</mtext><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>noise</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{\text{skip}}(t)\,\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t}+c_{\text{out}}(t)\,\text{NN}_{\bm{\theta}}\big(c_{\text{in}}(t)\,\mathbf{x}_{i}^{t},c_{\text{noise}}(t),\mathbf{z}_{i}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E9.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.E9.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{\text{skip}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>skip</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{\text{skip}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.E9.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{\text{data}}^{2}/({t^{2}+\sigma_{\text{data}}^{2}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>data</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>data</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{\text{data}}^{2}/({t^{2}+\sigma_{\text{data}}^{2}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E9.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.E9.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{\text{out}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{\text{out}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.E9.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(t\,\sigma_{\text{data}})/{\sqrt{t^{2}+\sigma_{\text{data}}^{2}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>data</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(t\,\sigma_{\text{data}})/{\sqrt{t^{2}+\sigma_{\text{data}}^{2}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9c)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E9.4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.E9.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{\text{in}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{\text{in}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.E9.4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1/{\sqrt{t^{2}+\sigma_{\text{data}}^{2}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>data</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1/{\sqrt{t^{2}+\sigma_{\text{data}}^{2}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9d)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E9.5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.E9.5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{\text{noise}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>noise</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{\text{noise}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A2.E9.5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{4}\ln t," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{4}\ln t,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9e)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{NN}_{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>NN</mtext><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{NN}_{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the actual neural network to be trained.
We set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{mean}}=-0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mean</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{mean}}=-0.4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{std}}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>std</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{std}}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> for a training noise sampling <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ln}~t\sim\mathcal{N}(P_{\text{mean}},P_{\text{std}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>ln</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mean</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>std</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ln}~t\sim\mathcal{N}(P_{\text{mean}},P_{\text{std}})</annotation></semantics></math> and network dropout rate of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib87" title="" class="ltx_ref">Srivastava et al., 2014</a>)</cite>.
The models are trained using the AdamW optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov &amp; Hutter, 2019</a>)</cite> for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">300</annotation></semantics></math>K training iterations.
Training is done on 8<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>NVIDIA H100 GPUs. Training duration is around <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="36" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>36</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">36</annotation></semantics></math> hrs.
Training is done with bf16.
The weight decay and momenta for AdamW are <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.02</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.02</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0.9,0.95)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0.9,0.95)</annotation></semantics></math>. We set a learning rate of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-4</annotation></semantics></math> with the constant learning rate scheduler, EMA rate of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9999</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9999</annotation></semantics></math>, and gradient clipping as <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
By default, we use a batch size of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math>.
To enable CFG sampling on the transformer, during training, we randomly replace all the video tokens <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i}(i=1,\dots,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i}(i=1,\dots,n)</annotation></semantics></math> with the learnable null embedding with the probability of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math>.
As our denoising network is not so large, we can sample <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> multiple times for any given <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We sample <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> times during training for each sample by following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. This operation helps improve the utilization of the loss function.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stage-2: ECT</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As same as Stage 1 network configuration, we utilize the EDM’s skip connection <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{skip}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>skip</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{skip}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, output scale <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{out}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{out}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, input scale <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{in}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{in}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{noise}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>noise</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{noise}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for modeling the head.
For a metric function <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, we use a Pseudo-Huber loss <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\mathbf{a},\mathbf{b})=\sqrt{\|\mathbf{a}-\mathbf{b}\|_{2}^{2}+\nu^{2}}-\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\mathbf{a},\mathbf{b})=\sqrt{\|\mathbf{a}-\mathbf{b}\|_{2}^{2}+\nu^{2}}-\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=0.06" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.06</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=0.06</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song &amp; Dhariwal, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geng et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>.
By following the original work, we set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{mean}}=-0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mean</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{mean}}=-0.8</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{std}}=1.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>std</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{std}}=1.6</annotation></semantics></math> for a training noise sampling <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ln}~t\sim\mathcal{N}(P_{\text{mean}},P_{\text{std}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>ln</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>mean</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>std</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ln}~t\sim\mathcal{N}(P_{\text{mean}},P_{\text{std}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(t)=1/t^{2}+1/\sigma_{\text{data}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>data</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(t)=1/t^{2}+1/\sigma_{\text{data}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the mapping function <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(r\mid t,\mathrm{Iters})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Iters</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(r\mid t,\mathrm{Iters})</annotation></semantics></math> (in Eq <a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Stage 2: Consistency fine-tuning via ECT ‣ 3.3 Training Framework ‣ 3 SoundReactor ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), we explore two different setups suggested by the literature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geng et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, which we describe in Section <a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>.
For <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CF</span> (our default), we set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s=\mathrm{total\_iter}//8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>total</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>iter</mi><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\mathrm{total\_iter}//8</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Stage 2: Consistency fine-tuning via ECT ‣ 3.3 Training Framework ‣ 3 SoundReactor ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). For <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">IN</span>, we set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s=\mathrm{total\_iter}//4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>total</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>iter</mi><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\mathrm{total\_iter}//4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math>.
The models are trained using the AdamW optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov &amp; Hutter, 2019</a>)</cite> for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math>K training iterations.
Training is done on 8<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>NVIDIA H100 GPUs. Training duration is around <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> hours.
Training is done with bf16.
The weight decay and momenta for AdamW are <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.02</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.02</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0.9,0.95)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0.9,0.95)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We set a learning rate of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-4</annotation></semantics></math> with the constant learning rate scheduler, EMA rate of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9999</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9999</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\text{sg}(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>sg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\text{sg}(\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi})}</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math>, and gradient clipping as <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
To enable CFG sampling, we randomly replace the learnable null embedding with all the video tokens <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i}(i=1,\dots,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i}(i=1,\dots,n)</annotation></semantics></math> with the probability of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math>. We sample <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> by 4 times during training for each sample by following the Stage 1 training.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Sampling Details</h3>

<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">AR transformer</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our sampling procedure follows that of a standard decoder-only AR transformer with a token-wise KV cache <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib81" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shazeer, 2019</a>)</cite>.
As described in Section <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Sampling Framework ‣ 3 SoundReactor ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, to get <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}</annotation></semantics></math> (a corresponding input token is a vision condition <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>), we apply CFG as <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}=\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}}+\omega(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{cond}}-\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>null</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>cond</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>null</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}=\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}}+\omega(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{cond}}-\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> is a guidance scale, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>cond</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the transformer output given the visual condition <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>null</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the output given a learnable null embedding, respectively.
To get <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>null</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}}</annotation></semantics></math>, all the <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{\leq i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\leq i}</annotation></semantics></math> are replaced with the learnable null embedding.
Sampling is done with bf16.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our approach contrasts with the CFG strategy in the original MAR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, where CFG is applied within the diffusion head.
In the original MAR, the transformer generates both conditional <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}^{\text{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}^{\text{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math> and unconditional <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}^{\text{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}^{\text{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math> vectors, which are then used for the standard CFG diffusion sampling.
In contrast, we do not apply CFG within the diffusion head. We compare the performance of both CFG strategies in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Ablation Study on Generator Training ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>.
Our design choice has a practical benefit, except for the performance: it reduces the computational overhead during sampling on the diffusion head, which might be critical when the head becomes larger or using the head without sampling acceleration.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Diffusion head</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the diffusion sampling on our Stage-1 model, we use the deterministic Heun solver with the same time-step discretizations as EDM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
Namely, if we generate samples with <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-steps, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}=(t_{\text{max}}^{1/\rho}+\frac{j}{N-1}(t_{\text{min}}^{1/\rho}-t_{\text{max}}^{1/\rho}))^{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mtext>min</mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ρ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}=(t_{\text{max}}^{1/\rho}+\frac{j}{N-1}(t_{\text{min}}^{1/\rho}-t_{\text{max}}^{1/\rho}))^{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=7</annotation></semantics></math>.
On our Stage-2 model, we set intermediate time step <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=2.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=2.5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=[5.0,1.1,0.08]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.08</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=[5.0,1.1,0.08]</annotation></semantics></math> on NFE=2 and NFE=4, respectively.
We use the EMA weights during sampling and set <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{\text{max}},t_{\text{min}}\}=\{80,0.00\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.00</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{\text{max}},t_{\text{min}}\}=\{80,0.00\}</annotation></semantics></math> on the both Stage-1 and Stage-
2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song &amp; Dhariwal, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geng et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>.
Sampling is done with bf16. We provide the sampling procedure in Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ A.2 AR Audio Generation without Vector Quantization ‣ Appendix A Related Work ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Context Window Extension on RoPE</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>, we test our model on longer sequence generation beyond the training context window up to twice the trainig window on SoundReactor-ECT with NFE=4.
In the experiments, we examine two zero-shot context window extension methods based on RoPE, Position Interpolation (PI) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and NTK-aware interpolation (NTK) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib91" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tancik et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, and Sliding Window Attention (SWA) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Beltagy et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
Here, we describe those methods.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">RoPE is applied to both the query (<math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math>) and key (<math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐤</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{k}</annotation></semantics></math>) vectors within a transformer layer. An input token <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is first projected into a query vector <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{i}=W_{q}\mathbf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{i}=W_{q}\mathbf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and a key vector <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{k}_{i}=W_{k}\mathbf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{k}_{i}=W_{k}\mathbf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{i},\mathbf{k}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{c_{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{i},\mathbf{k}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{c_{z}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To encode the positional information, the <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is treated as a sequence of two-dimensional vectors <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{i,2l-1},q_{i,2l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{i,2l-1},q_{i,2l})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> is the index ranging from <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathbf{z}}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathbf{z}}/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
A rotation is then applied to each pair as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}q^{\prime}_{i,2l-1}\\
q^{\prime}_{i,2l}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\cos i\varphi_{l}&amp;-\sin i\varphi_{l}\\
\sin i\varphi_{l}&amp;\cos i\varphi_{l}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}q_{i,2l-1}\\
q_{i,2l}\end{pmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}q^{\prime}_{i,2l-1}\\
q^{\prime}_{i,2l}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\cos i\varphi_{l}&amp;-\sin i\varphi_{l}\\
\sin i\varphi_{l}&amp;\cos i\varphi_{l}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}q_{i,2l-1}\\
q_{i,2l}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the frequency <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\varphi_{l}=\xi^{-2l/c_{\mathbf{z}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝐳</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{l}=\xi^{-2l/c_{\mathbf{z}}}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the index <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> and a base <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>. The same process is applied to the key vector <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{k}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{k}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Position interpolation (PI)</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">PI adapts RoPE to longer sequences by down-scaling the position indices via <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\prime}=i\cdot(n/n^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\prime}=i\cdot(n/n^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are a training sequence length and a target sequence length during inference, respectively. This operation uniformly compresses the entire frequency spectrum, which can degrade the model’s understanding of high-frequency details essential for precise temporal alignment.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">NTK-aware interpolation (NTK)</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Instead of scaling the position indices, NTK scales the base <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> of the frequency calculation to a new value <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi^{\prime}=\xi\cdot(n^{\prime}/n)^{c_{\mathbf{z}}/(c_{\mathbf{z}}-2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi^{\prime}=\xi\cdot(n^{\prime}/n)^{c_{\mathbf{z}}/(c_{\mathbf{z}}-2)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The approach is motivated by Neural Tangent Kernel theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib91" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tancik et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, which posits that deep neural networks have trouble learning high-frequency information if the input dimension is low without the corresponding embeddings having high-frequency components. NTK’s base rescaling allows the model to retain its modeling capabilities on high-frequency information, which we qualitatively observe in Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Effectiveness on frame-level online V2A generation ‣ 4.4 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sliding window attention (SWA)</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Besides extending the context window, SWA is one of the standard and efficient attention mechanisms that restricts each token to only attend to a fixed-size local window of preceding tokens. For generation beyond the training context window, it simply continues to apply this local attention window. While this approach is computationally efficient, its ability to model long-range dependencies is inherently limited by the fixed window size.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to quantitative evaluation in Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>, the spectrogram visualization in Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Effectiveness on frame-level online V2A generation ‣ 4.4 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows that PI slows periodic sounds (e.g., footsteps) and harms temporal synchronization, while NTK and SWA preserve timing.
We conjecture that this stems from how RoPE frequencies are scaled. Our interleaved, frame<span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>aligned audio–visual tokens rely on high<span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>frequency positional components for the precise timing of action sounds.
NTK rescales the RoPE base and preserves high<span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>frequency structure via <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi^{\prime}=\xi\cdot(n^{\prime}/n)^{c_{\mathbf{z}}/(c_{\mathbf{z}}-2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi^{\prime}=\xi\cdot(n^{\prime}/n)^{c_{\mathbf{z}}/(c_{\mathbf{z}}-2)}</annotation></semantics></math>. In contrast, PI stretches positions in the time domain <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\prime}=i\cdot(n/n^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\prime}=i\cdot(n/n^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, which lowers the angular frequency.
This experiment is complementary to prior findings from the other domains, such as language domain, by demonstrating the superiority of NTK over PI in a multimodal audio-visual setting. We validate its effectiveness through not only the quantitative performance difference but also the qualitative analysis of the spectrograms.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Per-frame Latency Measurement</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We measure two metrics: waveform-level and token-level latency.
Waveform-level latency is the elapsed time from feeding the previous audio token <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math> into the model until the output <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is incrementally decoded into a waveform, including the encoding of the raw video frame <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Token<span id="A2.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>level latency is identical to this but excludes the incremental waveform decoding.
Following Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ A.2 AR Audio Generation without Vector Quantization ‣ Appendix A Related Work ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we insert <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{torch.cuda.synchronize()}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚝𝚘𝚛𝚌𝚑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>𝚌𝚞𝚍𝚊</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>𝚜𝚢𝚗𝚌𝚑𝚛𝚘𝚗𝚒𝚣𝚎</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{torch.cuda.synchronize()}</annotation></semantics></math> calls between lines 2–3 and 14–15 to measure waveform-level latency, and between lines 2–3 and 11–12 to measure token<span id="A2.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>level latency.
This duration is recorded as the per-frame latency. For each video, we average the per-frame latencies over all frames except the initial one.
We perform this benchmark on a single H100 GPU with a batch size of one, using a single CUDA stream for the entire pipeline.
We use <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="53" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>53</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">53</annotation></semantics></math> clips (<math id="A2.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math>FPS, <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="480" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>480</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">480</annotation></semantics></math>p, <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> second) with the default SoundReactor<span id="A2.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>ECT at <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=3</annotation></semantics></math>. We use NTK to generate <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> seconds with KV-cache<span id="footnote10" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">10</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            NTK, PI, and no RoPE extension do not affect latency.</span></span></span>.
We apply FlashAttention-2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao, 2024</a>)</cite> for the main model.
The <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{torch.compile}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚝𝚘𝚛𝚌𝚑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>𝚌𝚘𝚖𝚙𝚒𝚕𝚎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{torch.compile}</annotation></semantics></math> is enabled on the main model while CUDA Graph is used on the VAE decoder.
We also enable the cuDNN auto-tuner (<math id="A2.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{cudnn.benchmark=True}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚌𝚞𝚍𝚗𝚗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>𝚋𝚎𝚗𝚌𝚑𝚖𝚊𝚛𝚔</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚃𝚛𝚞𝚎</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{cudnn.benchmark=True}</annotation></semantics></math>).
To measure the waveform-level latency, we use a causal stereo full-band VAE, which is trained by fine-tuning our default VAE to make the decoder causal while freezing the encoder parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the mean and standard deviation over the <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> clips following a <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-clip warm-up period<span id="footnote11" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">11</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">11</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">11</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            This is for excluding system warm-up effects, such as GPU kernel initialization.</span></span></span>.
As demonstrated in Table <a href="#S4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Generation beyond training context window ‣ 4.4 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, our model achieves both remarkably low per-frame token-level and waveform-level latency under NFE=1 to NFE=4 on the head.
In terms of sample quality, we observe that the causal VAE decoder lags behind its non<span id="A2.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>causal counterpart in reconstruction quality (causal: rMMD<math id="A2.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\text{OpenL3}}=62.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>OpenL3</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>62.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{OpenL3}}=62.7</annotation></semantics></math>, rMMD<math id="A2.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\text{CLAP}}=0.538" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>CLAP</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.538</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{CLAP}}=0.538</annotation></semantics></math>; non<span id="A2.SS5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>causal: rMMD<math id="A2.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\text{OpenL3}}=60.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>OpenL3</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>60.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{OpenL3}}=60.4</annotation></semantics></math>, rMMD<math id="A2.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\text{CLAP}}=0.301" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>CLAP</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.301</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{CLAP}}=0.301</annotation></semantics></math>).
This performance gap propagates to final generation quality: e.g., our model on ECT (NFE=4) with the causal decoder yields MMD<math id="A2.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\text{OpenL3}}=65.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>OpenL3</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>65.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{OpenL3}}=65.5</annotation></semantics></math> and MMD<math id="A2.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\text{CLAP}}=0.682" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>CLAP</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.682</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{CLAP}}=0.682</annotation></semantics></math>, versus <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64.6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.451" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.451</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.451</annotation></semantics></math> with the non-causal one (our default setup).
Accordingly, improving the fidelity of the causal VAE while keeping the decoding overhead small remains an important direction for future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.6 </span>Metrics Details</h3>

<section id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Audio quality</h5>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate audio quality, we use Frechet Audio Distance (FAD) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gui et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, Maximum Mean Discrepancy (MMD) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chung et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jayasumana et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and Kullback-Leibler divergence based on PaSST <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Koutini et al., 2022</a>)</cite> (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rm{KL}_{\text{PaSST}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>KL</mi><mtext>PaSST</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rm{KL}_{\text{PaSST}}</annotation></semantics></math>).
For FAD and MMD, following prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Evans et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Evans et al. (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gui et al. (2024)</a></cite>, we use OpenL3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cramer et al., 2019</a>)</cite> and LAION-CLAP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib105" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu* et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. For OpenL3, we use (Env, Mel256, 512) in <a href="https://github.com/torchopenl3/torchopenl3" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/torchopenl3/torchopenl3</a>. For CLAP, we use the <span id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">630k-audioset-fusion-best.pt</span> from <a href="https://github.com/LAION-AI/CLAP" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/LAION-AI/CLAP</a> as audio feature extractors.
Since our model is trained on stereo signals, we compute the metrics on four channel configurations: the left channel (Left), the right channel (Right), their average (Center), and their difference (Diff) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib88" title="" class="ltx_ref">Steinmetz et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.
We compute KL<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{PaSST}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>PaSST</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{PaSST}}</annotation></semantics></math> only on the Center.
For the samples from the models trained on monaural signal, they are duplicated for the left and right channels. Consequently, the Diff is omitted as the difference becomes zero.
Furthermore, as a complementary metric to evaluate stereo quality, we also use Frechet Stereo Audio Distance (FSAD) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which is based on StereoCRW <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2022b</a>)</cite> features.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Audio-visual alignment</h5>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate audio-visual semantic and temporal alignment, we utilize ImageBind score (IB-Score) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Girdhar et al., 2023</a>)</cite>
and DeSync <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib101" title="" class="ltx_ref">Viertola et al., 2025</a>)</cite> by following common practices <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib101" title="" class="ltx_ref">Viertola et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
To compute DeSync, we take two crops (first <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.8</annotation></semantics></math> sec. and last <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.8</annotation></semantics></math> sec.) from the video and compute the average over the results <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
We compute these two metrics only on the Center.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Experiments</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Ablation Study on Generator Training</h3>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Diffusion head size</h5>

<figure id="A3.T7" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:60%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Ablation study on various sizes of diffusion head on SoundReactor-Diffusion under a fixed entire network capacity. Bold and underlined scores indicate the best and second-best results, respectively.</figcaption>
