<td id="A3.T7.2.1.7.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A3.T7.2.1.7.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.03</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Table <a href="#A3.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Diffusion head size ‣ C.1 Ablation Study on Generator Training ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we analyze the capacity of the diffusion head while keeping the total model parameters fixed at <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="320" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>320</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">320</annotation></semantics></math> M parameters.
We use <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>35</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">35</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60\%</annotation></semantics></math>CEV) for this experiment.
A larger head consistently yields better generation quality.
Notably, while the original MAR generates valid images even with very small heads (e.g., <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>M and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>M parameters) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, our <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>M head variant failed to produce high-quality samples.
We hypothesize this is due to the challenge of handling high-dimensional audio tokens (<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathbf{x}}=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathbf{x}}=64</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="footnote12" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">12</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">12</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">12</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              A similar discussion has been reported in <a href="https://github.com/LTH14/mar/issues/55" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/LTH14/mar/issues/55</a>.</span></span></span>.
Indeed, our preliminary trials on an even higher dimension of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathbf{x}}=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathbf{x}}=128</annotation></semantics></math> yielded no valid audio even with a <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> M head.
Consequently, the necessity of allocating substantial capacity to the diffusion head directly slows down decoding speed per token, providing a strong motivation for the step-wise acceleration that we introduce in this work.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ECT strategy regarding fine-tuning component</h5>

<figure id="A3.T8" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:55%;">
