</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Ablation Study on Sampling Strategy</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we analyze the model’s behavior with various sampling strategies.
Figure <a href="#A3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ ECT strategy regarding fine-tuning component ‣ C.1 Ablation Study on Generator Training ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows the objective metrics for SoundReactor-Diffusion with various numbers of sampling steps, with the fixed guidance scale <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=3.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=3.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We observe that <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> steps (NFE=19) fail to generate valid samples, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> steps (NFE=39) begin to yield reasonable samples, and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math> (NFE=59) or more steps are required for high-quality samples. These results motivate us to conduct diffusion head acceleration to achieve low per-frame latency.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ ECT strategy regarding fine-tuning component ‣ C.1 Ablation Study on Generator Training ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we fix the number of steps to <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30</annotation></semantics></math> and examine the impact of the CFG scale <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>. The results indicate an optimal performance range between <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=2.0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=3.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=3.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We also include results from applying the original MAR’s CFG strategy to our models.
Concretely, <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}^{\text{cond}}=\texttt{Concat}(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i-1},\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{cond}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Concat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>cond</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}^{\text{cond}}=\texttt{Concat}(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i-1},\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{cond}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}^{\text{uncond}}=\texttt{Concat}(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i-1},\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>uncond</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Concat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>null</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}^{\text{uncond}}=\texttt{Concat}(\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i-1},\tilde{\mathbf{z}}_{2i}^{\text{null}})</annotation></semantics></math> are used to conduct CFG sampling on the diffusion head (See the difference from our strategy explained in Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ A.2 AR Audio Generation without Vector Quantization ‣ Appendix A Related Work ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and Appendix <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Sampling Details ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>).
While both strategies perform comparably, our approach is more computationally efficient, as noted in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Sampling Details ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, since our strategy does not use CFG on either diffusion or CM sampling.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A3.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ ECT strategy regarding fine-tuning component ‣ C.1 Ablation Study on Generator Training ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiments ‣ SoundReactor: Frame-level online video-to-audio generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> presents the objective metrics for SoundReactor-ECT across various NFEs and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> values. Similar to the results for SoundReactor-Diffusion, we observe a consistent performance sweet spot around <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=2.0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=3.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=3.0</annotation></semantics></math> for all evaluated NFEs on the head.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Ablation Study on Vision Conditioning</h3>

